" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Draža Mihailović</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Draža Mihailović was a Yugoslav army officer who led the royalist Chetnik movement in occupied Yugoslavia during the Second World War and served as minister of war of…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/the-dream-of-the-rood"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/the-dream-of-the-rood.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">The Dream of the Rood</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Dream of the Rood is an Old English poem in which the poet dreams of the Cross, which speaks of its part in Christ's crucifixion as a loyal retainer of a heroic lord.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/drenthe"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/drenthe.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Drenthe</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Drenthe is a province in the north-east of the Netherlands, with Assen as its capital.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/drepung-monastery"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/drepung-monastery.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Drepung Monastery</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Drepung Monastery, founded in 1416 by Jamyang Choje, a disciple of Tsongkhapa, lies on the outskirts of Lhasa in Tibet.</span></a></li></ul>
